     <h1 class="title" title="Lakkidi Hill Station">Lakkidi</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">

<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/south-india-hill-stations/lakkidi-hill-station.jpg" title="Lakkidi hill station" alt="Lakkidi hill station, hill stations in india, north india hill stations, Lakkidi" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Kerala<br />
<b>Area:</b> 129 sq.kms<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Gateway to Wayanad<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 700m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 25&#176;C to 29&#176;C, Winter 17&#176;C to 23&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to March</p>
<p><b>Lakkidi,</b> the <b>gateway of Wayanad</b>, is situated 700 m above mean sea level at the top of the ghat <b>Thamaraserri neck</b>. peaks, gurgling streams and luxuriant forests add magic to the journey up the winding roads of this mountain resort. Lakkidi is one of the places in <b>Wayanad</b>, and registers the <b>highest level of rainfall in the world</b>.</p>





